  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $69.8M in federal contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Agriculture recorded 986 awards with an average award size of $70.8K, and obligations fell 99.4% year over year. Historical annual obligations show larger totals in prior years: FY22 $10B, FY23 $11.5B, FY24 $11.6B, FY25 $9.6B, and FY26 $10.8B. Top spending categories in FY2027 to date include Logging $99.6M and Support Activities for Forestry $11.9M. Top vendors in FY2027 to date include PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC $99.6M and MICROSOFT CORPORATION $7.6M. The numbers above are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Use these figures for procurement analysis, vendor outreach, or market share benchmarking within the fiscal year to date window.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the FY2027 to date spending pattern?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $69.8M in FY2027 to date, a change that followed prior years of much larger annual obligations. The Department of Agriculture shows concentrated spending in certain categories, with Logging $99.6M and Support Activities for Forestry $11.9M listed among the top categories. The Department of Agriculture awarded 986 contracts, with an average award size of $70.8K, which reflects the mix of many smaller awards and a few large awards to named vendors."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the dominant vendors and categories right now?",
        "body": "PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC is the top vendor in FY2027 to date with $99.6M in obligations. Logging is the top category in FY2027 to date with $99.6M, followed by Support Activities for Forestry $11.9M and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services $7.6M. MICROSOFT CORPORATION is the next largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $7.6M, and other notable vendors include KONIAG TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS INC $5.2M and GUIDEHOUSE INC. $4M."
      }
    ]
  },
